--- !yfi/header
version: 1
namespace: edges::errors
visibility: public
--- !node &Alpha
pub port: 1
# `E0223` — an `!edge` with no `connections` relates nothing, and a tag that
# means nothing is worse than one that does not exist.
--- !edge &Bare
pub weight: 1
# `E0224` — `connections` must be a sequence of endpoints.
--- !edge &NotASequence
pub connections: 7
# `E0224` — `definition` must be a mapping of handles.
--- !edge &NotAMapping
pub connections: [Alpha]
pub definition: 1
# `E0225` twice — one handle past the end of `connections`, one that is not an
# index at all.
--- !edge &BadHandles
pub connections: [Alpha]
pub definition:
  source: 0
  target: 3
  other: nope
# `E0213` — a connections item is a reach, so an item naming nothing is the
# same failure a clause operand naming nothing is, with the same code.
--- !edge &Nowhere
pub connections: [Nothing]
# `E0213` twice, once for each spelling. An endpoint is a **node**; an anchored
# scalar is a value, and D6.1 makes only an anchored collection addressable. The
# path spelling has always said so, the alias spelling used to say nothing, and
# one question with two spellings had two answers.
--- !edge &ToAValue
pub limit: &limit 30
pub connections: [limit, *limit]
# `E0223` again, and worded for the case it is: this node writes the member
# itself. Nothing was inherited, so a message about a declaration nobody
# supplied would send the author looking for a base that does not exist.
--- !edge &Emptied
pub connections: ~
# A `connections` of the wrong shape removes the **bound** a handle is checked
# against, and nothing else. `connections` as a handle name and a value that is
# not a position at all are wrong however many endpoints there are, so both are
# `E0225` here; `late: 2` is not, because a position past the end of a sequence
# that was never read is a cascade from one fault rather than a fault of its
# own, and it goes away when the member above it is fixed.
--- !edge &Cascade
pub connections: 7
pub definition:
  connections: 0
  nope: what
  late: 2
# And `definition`'s own shape is a fault of its own: it is not a position in
# anything, so nothing about reading it depends on the member above it. Two
# members, two `E0224`s, from one node.
--- !edge &Both
pub connections: 7
pub definition: 1
